@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName DejaVu Sans

left to right direction
title Mapa de configuraciones y su impacto

package "Variables .env" {
  rectangle "DATA_DIR" as DATA_DIR
  rectangle "OUTPUT_DIR" as OUTPUT_DIR
  rectangle "TRAIN_BATCH_SIZE" as TRAIN_BATCH
  rectangle "TEST_BATCH_SIZE" as TEST_BATCH
  rectangle "MIXED_PRECISION" as MP
  rectangle "LOGGING_STEPS" as LOGS
  rectangle "CHECKPOINT_EPOCH" as CK_EPOCH
  rectangle "PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF" as CUDA_ALLOC
  rectangle "IDMVTON_LOW_RAM" as LOW_RAM
  rectangle "IDMVTON_CPU_OFFLOAD" as CPU_OFFLOAD
  rectangle "IDMVTON_FORCE_CPU" as FORCE_CPU
}

package "Efectos en el sistema" {
  rectangle "Consumo de VRAM" as VRAM
  rectangle "Latencia" as LAT
  rectangle "Estabilidad" as EST
  rectangle "Calidad visual" as QUAL
  rectangle "Costo de almacenamiento" as DISK
}

TRAIN_BATCH --> VRAM : alto impacto
TEST_BATCH --> VRAM : impacto medio
MP --> VRAM : reduce consumo
LOW_RAM --> VRAM : reduce pico
CPU_OFFLOAD --> VRAM : reduce pico
FORCE_CPU --> LAT : aumenta mucho
CUDA_ALLOC --> EST : reduce fragmentacion
LOGS --> LAT : puede aumentar picos
CK_EPOCH --> DISK : controla frecuencia
DATA_DIR --> EST : datos correctos
OUTPUT_DIR --> DISK : centraliza artefactos
LOW_RAM --> QUAL : posible perdida fina

note bottom
Lectura arquitectonica:
las variables no son solo parametros de IA;
son knobs de rendimiento, resiliencia operativa
y costo de infraestructura.
end note

@enduml